## Configuration

GenericAgent uses a `mykey.py` file in the project root for configuration. This file is auto-generated by the setup wizard, but you can also edit it manually:

```python
# mykey.py — Auto-generated by start.py

GA_LANG = "en"  # Interface language: en, fr, zh

# Anthropic Claude
native_claude_config = {
    'name': 'claude',
    'apikey': 'sk-ant-your-key-here',
    'apibase': 'https://api.anthropic.com',
    'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-6',
    'thinking_type': 'adaptive',
}

# OpenAI GPT
native_oai_config = {
    'name': 'gpt',
    'apikey': 'sk-your-key-here',
    'apibase': 'https://api.openai.com/v1',
    'model': 'gpt-4o',
    'api_mode': 'chat_completions',
}

# Auto-failover between providers
mixin_config = {
    'llm_nos': ['claude', 'gpt'],
    'max_retries': 5,
    'base_delay': 0.5,
}
```

Alternatively, you can use environment variables (see `.env.example`).

